  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Lost reopens; closed does not",
      "items": [
        "Reopening on the next use is what makes a retry possible \u2014 a new act under the same key",
        "close() may be called from any state; a closed link is never reopened behind the caller's back",
        "Every wait \u2014 CONNACK, PUBACK, ack, first-read grace \u2014 is bounded"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why we drop the session ourselves",
      "items": [
        "paho keeps an unacked QoS 1 message and re-sends it on reconnect with dup set",
        "A step that already returned Failed would then change the world later",
        "Dropping the client \u2014 DISCONNECT delivered, thread joined \u2014 is the only way the queue dies with it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What the step sees",
      "items": [
        "Refused or unreachable: Failed, nothing published, the link stays unopened",
        "No PUBACK: Failed, no receipt, and perhaps the command went out \u2014 that is what the key on the wire is for",
        "PUBACK but no ack: Failed, no receipt, and the link stays open \u2014 the command was certainly taken"
      ]
    }
  ]
